# POST /owners in the OfficeFloor PetClinic — Findings

## Base package & layout
- Base package: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic`
- Build tool: **Maven** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`; wrapper `./mvnw`). No explicit surefire/failsafe config, so the Spring Boot parent default runs `*Test.java` with **JUnit 5 (Jupiter)**. Run tests with `./mvnw test`.
- OfficeFloor endpoints are YAML pipelines under `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/`; escalation (error) handlers under `src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`. Function classes live in `.../rest/function/owner/`, escalation handlers in `.../rest/escalation/`.
- DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`, `PetDto`, …) are **generated** by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`). They are NOT checked-in source files — edit `openapi.yml` to change them.

## 1. POST /owners YAML
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RequireOwnerFields
  next: normalizeTelephone

normalizeTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```
Pipeline: `RequireOwnerFields → NormalizeOwnerTelephone → BuildOwner → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated`.

## 2. Function classes referenced by the POST YAML
All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`

**RequireOwnerFields.java** — reads raw `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (no `@Valid`), collects blank/missing required fields (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone), throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, else republishes the body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated`. (Full source read above.)

**NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java** — the only telephone normalization in the codebase:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
    String digits = request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "");
    if (digits.length() != 10) {
        throw new InvalidTelephoneException(
                "Telephone must be exactly 10 digits after removing non-digit characters");
    }
    request.setTelephone(digits);
}
```
Mutates the published `OwnerFieldsDto` in place (strips non-digits, requires exactly 10).

**BuildOwner.java**
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

**SaveOwner.java**
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

**RespondWithOwnerCreated.java**
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

Supporting mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct, `@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)`; `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`; `defaultComponentModel=spring`).

## 3. Entity & Repository
**Owner** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (extends `Person`, `@Entity @Table(name="owners")`). telephone field:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
Also `address`, `city` (`@NotEmpty`), and `@OneToMany ... Set<Pet> pets` (EAGER).

**OwnerRepository** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`. Methods: `findByLastName(String)`, `findByLastName(String, Pageable)`, `findById(int)`, `save(Owner)`, `findAll()`, `findAll(Pageable)`, `delete(Owner)`. There is **no** `findByTelephone`/uniqueness query.

Implementations (profile-selected): `.../repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (active — `spring-data-jpa` profile; `save` inherited from Spring Data `Repository`), `.../repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`.

## 4. DTOs
No hand-written owner DTOs exist. They are generated from `openapi.yml`. Schema for `OwnerFields` (→ `OwnerFieldsDto`) at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 1991–2039: string fields firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; telephone `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'`, minLength 1, maxLength 20; all five `required`. `Owner` (→ `OwnerDto`, lines 2040–2063) = `allOf OwnerFields` + `id` (readOnly int) + `pets` (readOnly array, required). `OwnerPage` (→ `OwnerPageDto`) at 2064+.

## 5. Escalation handlers (owner-related)
YAMLs under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/` map an exception FQN → a handler class. Relevant to owner creation:

- `...InvalidTelephoneException.yml` → `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneHandler`
- `...MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml` → `MissingOwnerFieldsHandler`
- `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` → `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler`
- `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` → `ValidationExceptionHandler`
- Also present: `NotFoundException.yml`→`NotFoundExceptionHandler`, `java.lang.Exception.yml`→`GeneralExceptionHandler`, `...AuthorizationDeniedException.yml`.

Handler Java classes (all in `.../rest/escalation/`):

**MissingOwnerFieldsException.java** — carries `List<String> fields` (immutable copy), message "Missing or blank required fields: ...".
**MissingOwnerFieldsHandler.java** — responds **400** with body `Map.of("errors", ex.getFields())`.
**InvalidTelephoneException.java** — simple message-only `Exception`.
**InvalidTelephoneHandler.java** — responds **400** with `ex.getMessage()` as plain body.
**DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler.java** — note it currently responds **404 NOT_FOUND** (via `ProblemDetails.build(...)`), not 409:
```java
public void handle(@Parameter DataIntegrityViolationException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response) {
    ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "...data constraint violation");
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(detail));
}
```
Other handlers present but not yet read in detail: `ValidationExceptionHandler.java`, `NotFoundExceptionHandler.java`, `GeneralExceptionHandler.java`, `ForbiddenExceptionHandler.java`, `ProblemDetails.java` (helper).

## 6. Telephone storage & normalization
- Stored on `Owner.telephone` as a `String`, DB column `owners.telephone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL` (h2 `schema.sql` lines 31–38; hsqldb/mysql/postgres analogous). **No UNIQUE constraint** on telephone in any schema; only `CREATE INDEX idx_owners_last_name`.
- Entity-level validation: exactly 10 digits (`@Pattern ^[0-9]{10}$`, `@Digits`).
- The ONLY normalization is `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` (strip `\D`, require 10 digits) in the POST pipeline. Grep for "telephone"/"normaliz" across `src` found matches only in: the two acceptance test files, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, `InvalidTelephoneException`/`Handler`, `RequireOwnerFields`, `ApplyOwner`, `Owner.java`, and JDBC repo SQL. There is no telephone-uniqueness / duplicate-detection logic anywhere.

## 7. Tests
Test tree: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/` — three files: `AcceptanceBase.java`, `AcceptanceTest.java`, `AuditLogCapture.java`. JUnit 5 + `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN)`; drives everything through `MockMvc` on `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` (uses Jackson 3 `tools.jackson.databind`).

**AcceptanceTest.java** (the tests hitting POST /owners):
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
  @Test void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
    createOwnerOk(a);
    ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
    b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
    createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());   // expects 409
  }
  @Test void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
    createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
  }
}
```
Key helpers in **AcceptanceBase.java** (full source read above): `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner; `uniqueTelephone()` = `String.format("04%08d", seq())` (10 digits); `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk` POST to `/api/owners`; `getOwner`/`fetchOwner` GET; `extractId` reads `id` from body or the `Location` header.

Test datasource: `src/test/resources/application.properties` sets `spring.profiles.active=hsqldb,spring-data-jpa`, `context-path=/petclinic/`, security enabled.

## Note relevant to your likely task
The acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expects **409 Conflict** on a duplicate normalized telephone, but the current POST pipeline has **no uniqueness check**, there is **no DB unique constraint** on telephone, and the only handler that could fire on a constraint violation (`DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler`) currently returns **404, not 409**. So implementing the telephone-unique rule will require adding a check/step (and/or a 409 handler) — none exists yet.

